<task_report_context>
  <instruction>Generate a comprehensive evaluation report for the user's task</instruction>

  <user_task>
    <input>{{.Task.Input}}</input>
  </user_task>

  {{if .Tasks}}
  <previous_tasks>
    {{range .Tasks}}
    <task>
      <id>{{.ID}}</id>
      <input>{{.Input}}</input>
      <status>{{.Status}}</status>
      <result>{{.Result}}</result>
    </task>
    {{end}}
  </previous_tasks>
  {{end}}

  {{if .CompletedSubtasks}}
  <completed_subtasks>
    {{range .CompletedSubtasks}}
    <subtask>
      <id>{{.ID}}</id>
      <title>{{.Title}}</title>
      <description>{{.Description}}</description>
      <status>{{.Status}}</status>
      <result>{{.Result}}</result>
    </subtask>
    {{end}}
  </completed_subtasks>
  {{end}}

  {{if .PlannedSubtasks}}
  <planned_subtasks>
    {{range .PlannedSubtasks}}
    <subtask>
      <id>{{.ID}}</id>
      <title>{{.Title}}</title>
      <description>{{.Description}}</description>
    </subtask>
    {{end}}
  </planned_subtasks>
  {{else}}
  <planned_subtasks status="empty">
    <message>All subtasks have been completed. Review their statuses and results to prepare your report.</message>
  </planned_subtasks>
  {{end}}

  {{if .ExecutionState}}
  <execution_state>
  {{.ExecutionState}}
  </execution_state>
  {{end}}

  {{if .ExecutionLogs}}
  <execution_logs>
  {{.ExecutionLogs}}
  </execution_logs>
  {{end}}
</task_report_context>


## REPRODUCIBLE TEST EVIDENCE
For each test, include in the engagement language: target endpoint and method; objective; numbered steps actually performed; baseline versus test variant; evidence source path or execution log identifier.
Embed the actual sanitized request in a fenced http block (request line, Host, relevant headers and body), and the corresponding response in a separate fenced http block (status, relevant headers, body excerpt and request ID). For command-line tests include the actual command in a bash block and observed output. Explain expected behavior, observed behavior and the evidence-based verdict. A file path alone is insufficient.
Only label requests as executed when supported by execution logs or retrieved evidence. Label illustrative payloads as examples. Missing response, WAF logs, callback or business-effect evidence means not verified. HTTP 200 alone does not prove exploitation. Never invent requests, responses, timestamps, screenshots or successful exfiltration.
Redact credentials, session cookies, tokens, secrets and personal data from headers, URLs and bodies. For out-of-band tests include only observed callbacks and sanitized test markers, never real session data.
